  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene01> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene01> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene01> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "A laboratory needs to compare three solid-phase extraction methods, abbreviated SPE. The response is recovery, recorded in percent. Each method is represented by six independently prepared river-water samples. These are illustrative synthetic measurements, not evidence from a real laboratory study. The experimental unit is a preparation, not an injection of an extract that has already been prepared. Our decision concerns the population mean recovery associated with each method under the stated conditions. Three observed means are a starting point, not a complete answer. We first need to see the observations and understand how much variation remains within each method."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-02> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-02-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-02-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene02> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "Ask how many groups are visible in panels A, B and C before revealing their construction. All panels contain three groups with the same centres and axes. Within-group scatter decreases from left to right. Invite students to explain what made their count uncertain and which panel first made separate clouds plausible. The centres are identical in all three panels. The spread around each centre makes the difference. On the next slide we will change that spread ourselves and compare it with the separation between the means."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-03> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene03> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "Compare A with B, A with C, and B with C using the original river-water data. Each pooled t-test divides the difference of two sample means by its standard error. Take both tails of the t distribution with ten degrees of freedom. Multiply each raw p-value by three and cap it at one. Read each pair once in the upper triangle. A versus B and B versus C cross the adjusted threshold of 0.05. A versus C does not. Next consider what these decisions can and cannot tell us."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-04> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene04> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "One-way analysis of variance, or ANOVA, asks whether all group population means are equal. Here the factor is the SPE method, with three levels called A, B and C. The null hypothesis states that the population mean recovery is the same at all three levels. The alternative says that at least one population mean differs from another. It does not require all three means to differ. Although its name mentions variance, the purpose of this classical test is to compare means by studying different components of observed variation. Next we connect these components to the experimental units and measurements that produced them."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-05> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-05-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-05-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-05-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-05-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene05> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "Follow one independently prepared sample through the experiment. A method is applied during preparation, and the resulting recovery is measured in percent. The factor is method; its levels are A, B and C; the response is recovery. The observation notation identifies both the method group and the preparation within that group. Six injections from one extract would assess a different source of variation and would not create six independent preparations. Replication must therefore be understood from the design, not inferred from the number of instrument readings. With these roles clear, we can ask how variability among observations relates to variability among group means."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-06> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-06-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-06-2> .

  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene06> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "All eighteen original synthetic river-water preparations belong to one collection, but each observation also belongs to its method group. Ignoring method gives one overall cloud around a grand mean. Retaining method reveals scatter within each group as well as separation among their centers. These are different descriptions of the same observations, not newly generated datasets. Even if the methods had identical population means, independent preparations would still vary. ANOVA compares the separation of estimated group centers with that remaining scatter. Before calculating this comparison, we need to distinguish departures from a group mean from departures from the grand mean."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-08> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-08-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-08-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-08-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-08-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene08> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "Consider the original observation R-A-01, whose recovery is 93 percent. Its method A sample mean is 94 percent and the grand mean is 95 percent. Relative to the grand mean, the observation is two percentage points lower. This total departure consists of a one-percentage-point departure below its group mean and a group mean that is itself one percentage point below the grand mean. The signed pieces add to the signed total. The displayed identity applies to every observation, not just this example. Squaring and summing these departures will lead to the between-group and within-group decomposition, but that next step needs a justification."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-09> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-09-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-09-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-09-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-09-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene09> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "For each preparation, split the departure from the grand mean into a residual around its group mean and a departure of that group mean from the grand mean. Squaring introduces a mixed term. Within each group, the residuals sum to zero because the group mean was calculated from those same observations. The group-mean departure is constant within that group, so it can be taken outside the inner sum. The mixed term therefore vanishes after summation. This explains why the total sum of squares equals the between-group sum plus the within-group sum. For the original synthetic river data, the three values are 114, 84 and 30 percentage points squared."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-10> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-10-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-10-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-10-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-10-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene10> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "A sum of squares must be interpreted together with its degrees of freedom. Eighteen observations have seventeen independent departures around their fitted grand mean because those departures sum to zero. Three fitted group means supply two independent contrasts once the grand mean constraint is accounted for. Within each group, estimating one mean leaves five independent residual departures among six preparations. Across three groups, that gives fifteen residual degrees of freedom. The total seventeen therefore splits into two between-group and fifteen within-group degrees of freedom. This counting explains why the two sums of squares need different divisors before we compare them."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-11> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-11-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-11-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-11-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-11-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene11> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "The original synthetic river-water data have a between-group sum of squares of 84 and a within-group sum of squares of 30, both in percentage points squared. Dividing each by its own degrees of freedom gives a mean square. The between-group calculation divides 84 by two to give 42. The within-group calculation divides 30 by fifteen to give two. Under the common-variance error model, the within-group mean square estimates the shared error variance. These mean squares are not additive in the way the sums of squares are. Their role is to place the two sources of variation on a comparable scale before forming a ratio."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-concept-12> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-12-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-12-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-12-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-12-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene12> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "The F statistic divides the between-group mean square by the within-group mean square. For the original synthetic river-water data this is 42 divided by two, giving 21. Both mean squares use percentage points squared, so the ratio has no unit. Under equal population means, independent Normal errors with a common positive variance give an F reference distribution with numerator degrees of freedom two and denominator degrees of freedom fifteen. The statistic alone does not supply a probability without those degrees of freedom and assumptions. A zero error mean square leaves the ratio undefined under our teaching convention. We can now explore which changes increase or decrease F."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-01-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-01-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-01-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-02-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-02-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-03-4> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-intro-item-04-4> .
